<title>USA: Seymour, Wis., won by Bankers' Bank. [CORRECTED 16:40 GMT]</title>
<headline>Seymour, Wis., won by Bankers' Bank. [CORRECTED 16:40 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects company name in headline and throughout to Bankers' Bank, from Griffin Kubik, Stephens &amp; Thompson, Inc.)</p>
<p>Bankers' Bank  said Monday it won $1.625 million of Seymour, Wis., general obligation promissory notes, with a true interest cost of 4.96 percent (corrects from 5.00 percent).  </p>
<p>AMT: 1,625,000	DATE: 09/23/96	NYC Time: 1200     CUSIP: 818767</p>
<p>ISSUER: Seymour							  ST: WI</p>
<p>ISSUE: General Obligation Promissory Notes		     TAX STAT: Exempt-ULT</p>
<p>M/SP/F: NR/NR/NA							 BOOK ENTRY: Y</p>
<p>ENHANCEMENTS: None						     BANK QUAL: Y</p>
<p>DTD: 10/01/96							    SURE BID: Y</p>
<p>DUE: 10/1/97-03					     SR MGR: Bankers Bank</p>
<p>1ST CPN: 04/01/97					   DOLLAR BID: 99.64</p>
<p>CALL: 10/1/00 @ par					 TIC 4.96</p>
<p>DELIVERY: 40 days					   ORDERS: NA</p>
<p>PAYING AGENT: City Clerk/Treasurer's Office, Seymour</p>
<p>L.O.: Quarles &amp; Brady, Milwaukee</p>
<p>F.A.: Ehlers and Associates, Inc., Minneapolis</p>
<p>LAST SALE: $1,600,000 3/9/92 @ 5.73100% NIC; 6yrs 4mos Avg; BBI-6.71%</p>
<p>Year		     Amount    Coupon     Yield     Price  Conc.</p>
<p>1997		    175,000     4.300	NRO		  NRO</p>
<p>1998		    175,000     4.550	NRO		  NRO</p>
<p>1999		    175,000     4.700	NRO		  NRO</p>
<p>2000		    200,000     4.800	NRO		  NRO</p>
<p>2001		    300,000     4.900	NRO		  NRO</p>
<p>2002		    300,000     4.950	NRO		  NRO</p>
<p>2003		    300,000     5.000	NRO		  NRO</p>
